      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "text": "In general, spoken statements are the major way of communication, but body language and facial expressions also have such kinds of function. For example, yawning means not being interested and turning one’s back to someone or swinging your fist shows your anger. But what those gestures really mean is subjective in different cultures.",
        "zh": "一般来说，口头表达是主要的交流方式，但肢体语言和面部表情也具有这类功能。比如，打哈欠表示不感兴趣，而背对着某人，或者挥动拳头，则表示你生气了。但在不同文化里，这些手势的真正含义带有主观性。",
        "start": 3.56,
        "voiceEnd": 30.356666666666666,
        "end": 57.153333333333336,
